  "description": "<p>The fedora ontology at: <a href=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository</a> contains triples for owl:Individual, but AFAIK, this is not a valid owl property (it isn't in the spec for the owl v2 schema: <a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#</a>). These triples are not visible in the HTML view, so you must use `curl` to request the application/rdf+xml representation in order to see these values.</p>\n\n<p>It is quite possible that owl:NamedIndividual is meant for the \"active\" and \"deleted\" values so that the ontology would read like this:</p>\n\n<p>   &lt;owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#active\"&gt;<br/>\n     &lt;rdfs:label xml:lang=\"en\"&gt;active&lt;/rdfs:label&gt;<br/>\n     &lt;rdfs:comment xml:lang=\"en\"&gt;The resource is active.&lt;/rdfs:comment&gt;<br/>\n     &lt;rdf:type rdf:resource=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#ResourceStatus\"/&gt;<br/>\n   &lt;/owl:NamedIndividual&gt;<br/>\n   &lt;owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#deleted\"&gt;<br/>\n     &lt;rdfs:label xml:lang=\"en\"&gt;deleted&lt;/rdfs:label&gt;<br/>\n     &lt;rdfs:comment xml:lang=\"en\"&gt;The resource has been marked for deletion.&lt;/rdfs:comment&gt;<br/>\n     &lt;rdf:type rdf:resource=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#ResourceStatus\"/&gt;<br/>\n   &lt;/owl:NamedIndividual&gt;</p>",
